WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.080 --> 00:00:05.380
Hey youtubers it’s Charlie, hopefully you
guys have had a chance to see Listen this

00:00:05.380 --> 00:00:06.380
weekend.

00:00:06.380 --> 00:00:11.000
Since it was somewhat of a horror story, I
thought it would be fun to talk about favorite

00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:12.490
Scary episodes.

00:00:12.490 --> 00:00:15.740
Horror is kind of subjective, but I feel like
there are at least a few episodes everyone

00:00:15.740 --> 00:00:18.500
can agree on being really scary.

00:00:18.500 --> 00:00:23.570
Imagine what Doctor Who would have looked
like had Christopher Lee become one of the

00:00:23.570 --> 00:00:24.900
Doctors in the early years.

00:00:24.900 --> 00:00:27.790
It would have been the stuff of nightmares.

00:00:27.790 --> 00:00:31.210
And quick reminder, this week’s giveaway
is still running.

00:00:31.210 --> 00:00:35.860
All you have to do to enter is be a subscriber
and leave a comment.

00:00:35.860 --> 00:00:37.210
I’ll pick a winner in my Q&amp;A tomorrow.

00:00:37.210 --> 00:00:42.260
So Top 5 Scary Episodes, Number 5 - Family
Of Blood

00:00:42.260 --> 00:00:45.110
Shout out to Harry Lloyd for being such an
amazing creeper.

00:00:45.110 --> 00:00:49.230
There’s something about Doctor Who period
episodes that makes them feel scarier.

00:00:49.230 --> 00:00:51.780
Maybe because everything looks less familiar.

00:00:51.780 --> 00:00:57.040
The monsters from Listen this week remind
me a little of the scarecrow monsters in that

00:00:57.040 --> 00:00:59.790
they are relatively features and they don’t
speak.

00:00:59.790 --> 00:01:02.970
I definitely think it’s scarier when Monsters
don’t say anything.

00:01:02.970 --> 00:01:10.190
One of my favorite props in the episode is
the red balloon Sister Mine carries around.

00:01:10.190 --> 00:01:13.960
The episode is also really notable for it’s
use of the Doctor’s Time Lord fob watch.

00:01:13.960 --> 00:01:15.620
They take his essence, completely neutralizing
him.

00:01:15.620 --> 00:01:20.330
And after it’s all over, the Doctor ends
up looking like the monster.

00:01:20.330 --> 00:01:23.650
Here were the punishments he handed out to
the Family of Blood.

00:01:23.650 --> 00:01:26.080
Sister Mine was forever trapped in the mirror.

00:01:26.080 --> 00:01:31.000
Mother would be forever falling into a star,
Father forever wrapped in chains and Brother

00:01:31.000 --> 00:01:33.780
forever a scarecrow in the field.

00:01:33.780 --> 00:01:36.220
All because they wanted to live forever.

00:01:36.220 --> 00:01:42.500
It’s like the Doctor is a Jinn and he grants
them their wishes but in a really twisted

00:01:42.500 --> 00:01:43.970
effed up way.

00:01:43.970 --> 00:01:45.630
Number 4 - Brain of Morbius

00:01:45.630 --> 00:01:50.180
This is a fourth Doctor Story involving a
battle with renegade Time Lord Morbius.

00:01:50.180 --> 00:01:54.650
I think of it as being a twist on the classic
Frankenstein story wherein the Monster eventually

00:01:54.650 --> 00:01:56.490
turns on his master.

00:01:56.490 --> 00:02:00.790
The classic episodes in general used a lot
of creepy organ and synthesizer music, which

00:02:00.790 --> 00:02:02.330
i feel help put you on edge.

00:02:02.330 --> 00:02:07.180
For younger people, think of the soundtracks
like old X-Files episodes.

00:02:07.180 --> 00:02:08.739
Where it’s like really creepy tonal music.

00:02:08.739 --> 00:02:11.230
Some interesting behind the scenes facts.

00:02:11.230 --> 00:02:17.910
This is one of the few stories where a gunshot
is heard and blood is seen pouring from a

00:02:17.910 --> 00:02:18.910
wound.

00:02:18.910 --> 00:02:26.660
There was a reference to the Doctor not carrying
a gun in Listen this week.

00:02:26.660 --> 00:02:31.800
The Doctor Frankenstein of the episode is
Doctor Solon, who takes the hand of his servant

00:02:31.800 --> 00:02:35.090
Condo, who already kind of looks scary.

00:02:35.090 --> 00:02:38.000
And sews it on to Morbius.

00:02:38.000 --> 00:02:42.730
When the servant realizes what’s happened
and that Solon replaced his taken hand with

00:02:42.730 --> 00:02:46.520
a hook, he shoots condo in the chest a bunch
of times.

00:02:46.520 --> 00:02:47.520
Thus the blood.

00:02:47.520 --> 00:02:50.670
Much more violent than I can ever remember
modern who being.

00:02:50.670 --> 00:02:53.020
Number 3 - Caves of Androzani

00:02:53.020 --> 00:02:55.209
This was the Fifth Doctor’s final story.

00:02:55.209 --> 00:03:00.641
The villain Jek had this nightmare-inducing
costume and makeup so not only did he look

00:03:00.641 --> 00:03:06.470
scary in a post-Star Wars Burned Face Darth
Vader way, but he was utterly insane.

00:03:06.470 --> 00:03:09.140
Him creeping on Peri just makes you shiver.

00:03:09.140 --> 00:03:16.099
It’s hard to tell if he wants to be with
her or if he wants to eat her for dinner.

00:03:16.099 --> 00:03:21.050
It’s like a Buffalo Bill Silence of the
Lambs thing where he feels like a serial killer.

00:03:21.050 --> 00:03:23.910
So you can’t apply normal logic to his actions.

00:03:23.910 --> 00:03:29.610
To be fair Jek is a villain of circumstance.

00:03:29.610 --> 00:03:32.131
So you do feel a little bit of sympathy for
him.

00:03:32.131 --> 00:03:35.610
But the who story is one of the darkest regenerations
ever.

00:03:35.610 --> 00:03:37.470
That would make a list.

00:03:37.470 --> 00:03:40.331
Rank the doctor’s regenerations from Happiest
to Darkest.

00:03:40.331 --> 00:03:47.690
It feels like all the modern who regenerations
have been hopeful positive moments.

00:03:47.690 --> 00:03:48.690
So Classic Who would just dominate.

00:03:48.690 --> 00:03:50.160
Number 2 - Empty Child

00:03:50.160 --> 00:03:55.740
I feel like a lot of the tumblr reaction gif
sets use Empty Child gas mask pics just for

00:03:55.740 --> 00:03:56.879
the shock value.

00:03:56.879 --> 00:04:07.650
The tone of the episode works really well
with the intensity of 

00:04:07.650 --> 00:04:08.650
the 9th Doctor.

00:04:08.650 --> 00:04:16.130
And there was this really cool blending of
a futuristic technovirus with World War 2

00:04:16.130 --> 00:04:17.130
set decoration.

00:04:17.130 --> 00:04:21.400
I do a lot of Walking Dead videos and Robert
Kirman tells amazing Zombie Stories, but I

00:04:21.400 --> 00:04:25.710
feel like Doctor Who’s techno Zombies were
a good twist on the genre.

00:04:25.710 --> 00:04:31.949
Ever since George Romero created the genre
with Dawn of the Dead, almost everything has

00:04:31.949 --> 00:04:33.370
been a riff on his zombies.

00:04:33.370 --> 00:04:39.110
So I always give extra points to stories like
Empty Child that can tell a unique zombie

00:04:39.110 --> 00:04:40.110
story.

00:04:40.110 --> 00:04:47.479
And the end when the Doctor puts on the gas
mask and repeats the “Are you my mummy”

00:04:47.479 --> 00:04:49.849
line.

00:04:49.849 --> 00:04:53.469
It feels like the mean type of joke they’d
give to Capaldi.

00:04:53.469 --> 00:04:57.949
Although his dark sense of humor is a little
less insane than the 9th Doctors.

00:04:57.949 --> 00:05:01.259
There’s something about the 9th Doctor that
made him feel like the craziest of all the

00:05:01.259 --> 00:05:03.289
new who doctors.

00:05:03.289 --> 00:05:07.279
He was fresh from the war, so he was just
starting to deal with what he’d done.

00:05:07.279 --> 00:05:11.199
Like he was still in shock, so he had a much
harder time approximating normal human social

00:05:11.199 --> 00:05:12.199
behavior.

00:05:12.199 --> 00:05:21.159
And my Number 1 Scary Doctor Who Episode - Blink

00:05:21.159 --> 00:05:25.449
Weeping Angels, hands down my own personal
favorite scary monster.

00:05:25.449 --> 00:05:29.960
How do you avoid something when your body
forces you to Blink?

00:05:29.960 --> 00:05:31.159
It’s almost impossible.

00:05:31.159 --> 00:05:35.111
And a lot of times, I feel like the Doctor
and his companions have only escaped the angels

00:05:35.111 --> 00:05:46.960
because they’ve been in a group of people
and the Angels nab the red shirts.

00:05:46.960 --> 00:05:50.620
I feel like a lot of the brilliance of the
episode comes from the macguffin, the VHS

00:05:50.620 --> 00:05:54.800
tapes that the Doctor uses to communicate
and the execution of the angels themselves.

00:05:54.800 --> 00:06:03.080
Part of the fun is that the angels don’t
talk, unless you count Angel bob, and they

00:06:03.080 --> 00:06:09.689
don’t move when either the characters or
we the audience are looking at them.

00:06:09.689 --> 00:06:13.729
For instance, usually when the angels move
on camera, it’s while the camera isn’t

00:06:13.729 --> 00:06:14.729
on them.

00:06:14.729 --> 00:06:18.900
Or when a video feed a character in the episode
is watching cuts out.

00:06:18.900 --> 00:06:20.399
The teeth and claws too.

00:06:20.399 --> 00:06:24.979
Whenever I watch supernatural now and see
the human angels like castiel walking around,

00:06:24.979 --> 00:06:29.499
I still think of their actual appearance as
being more like the weeping angels.

00:06:29.499 --> 00:06:37.780
I don’t expect them back in Series 8, just
because they were used during the christmas

00:06:37.780 --> 00:06:42.160
special and all over Matt Smith’s run.

